00:19:40,961 --> 00:19:44,960
pressure to crack the heavier hydrocarbons that wouldn't break

338
00:19:44,961 --> 00:19:49,400
heavier hydrocarbons that wouldn't break before.

339
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:53,460
Following another trip through a fractionating tower, gasoline

340
00:19:53,560 --> 00:20:00,100
yields from a barrel of oil went from about 45% to over 50%.

341
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:03,720
The greatest advantage that the Allied forces had in World War

342
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:06,920
II was an abundance of petroleum and petroleum

343
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:09,720
products versus the Japanese and the Germans.

344
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:13,260
Almost immediately after the beginning of hostilities,

345
00:20:13,261 --> 00:20:16,560
The industry was organized under the government to greatly

346
00:20:16,660 --> 00:20:18,660
