00:21:41,361 --> 00:21:44,920
And all of this is connected by a spaghetti bowl of pipes,

370
00:21:44,921 --> 00:21:47,920
heading off in all directions.

371
00:21:47,921 --> 00:21:50,900
But there is a method to the seeming madness.

372
00:21:50,901 --> 00:21:52,900
It really does follow a flow.

373
00:21:52,901 --> 00:21:56,060
You can follow the flow of crude oil coming in.

374
00:21:56,061 --> 00:21:58,060
It then goes to certain processes,

375
00:21:58,061 --> 00:22:00,300
depending on how it's separated.

376
00:22:00,301 --> 00:22:03,380
And the reason that there are so many pipes going

377
00:22:03,381 --> 00:22:05,780
around the refinery is that we have

378
00:22:05,781 --> 00:22:09,220
to keep all those products separate.

379
00:22:09,221 --> 00:22:11,280
After arriving by tanker ship at the dock

380
00:22:11,281 --> 00:22:15,620
from the large oil fields of the world in Alaska, Mexico,

381
00:22:15,621 --> 00:22:18,560
Venezuela, and the Middle East, crude oil

382
00:22:18,561 --> 00:22:21,920
